  "source": "https://gc.nh.gov/rsa/html/LXIII/660/660-24.htm",
  "statuteText": "660:24 State Offices in State General Elections. –\n\nIf the candidates having the highest number of votes for the office of governor, councilor, state senator, or state representative shall have an equal number, the choice shall be made as provided in the state constitution. Such candidate chosen shall then be declared duly elected."
}
